The most dangerous failure coupling is between the ISRU power failure and the life support system. During a global dust storm, solar power fails. The Kilopower reactor takes 4 hours to reach criticality from cold start. The 300 kWh battery provides 4 × 75 kW = 4 h × 75 kW life support power, exactly matching the reactor startup time. This creates a zero-margin coupling that must be resolved: the battery must be sized to 360 kWh (20% margin) or the reactor must be maintained in hot standby during storm season.

