## A.1 Notation and Conventions

Throughout all appendices the following notation is standard and fixed.

Scalars are denoted by italic lowercase letters: a, b, t, x. Vectors are bold lowercase: **x**, **u**, **e**. Matrices are bold uppercase: **A**, **K**, **P**. Sets are calligraphic uppercase: S, C, M. The Euclidean norm of a vector **v** ∈ R^n is ||**v**|| = sqrt(**v**^T **v**). The Frobenius norm of a matrix **M** ∈ R^{m×n} is ||**M**||_F = sqrt(tr(**M**^T **M**)). The spectral radius of **A** is ρ(**A**) = max{|λ| : λ ∈ eigenvalues(**A**)}. The symbol ∇f(**x**) denotes the column gradient vector of scalar f at **x**. The symbol ∂f/∂**x** denotes the Jacobian matrix (row gradient when f is a vector). The symbol ⊗ denotes the Kronecker product. The symbol ⊕ denotes direct sum of vector spaces. The symbol ∧ is logical AND, ∨ is logical OR, ¬ is logical NOT. Temporal logic operators: F ("eventually"), G ("always"), X ("next"), U ("until"). The indicator function 1[A] = 1 if condition A is true, 0 otherwise.

