## M.2 Out-of-Distribution Detection — Mathematical Specification

**Gaussian Mixture Model Fit:**

The GMM is fitted to latent space codes {**z**_1,...,**z**_N_train} from nominal training data. The GMM has K = 16 components:

p(**z**) = Σ_{k=1}^{16} π_k · N(**z**; μ_k, Σ_k)

Parameters {π_k, μ_k, Σ_k} are estimated by the EM algorithm:

**E-step:** Compute responsibilities r_{nk} = π_k N(**z**_n; μ_k, Σ_k) / Σ_j π_j N(**z**_n; μ_j, Σ_j)

**M-step:**
π_k^{new} = (1/N) Σ_n r_{nk}
μ_k^{new} = Σ_n r_{nk} **z**_n / Σ_n r_{nk}
Σ_k^{new} = Σ_n r_{nk}(**z**_n−μ_k^{new})(**z**_n−μ_k^{new})^T / Σ_n r_{nk}

EM is run to convergence (change in log-likelihood < 10^{−4}).

**OOD Score:**

score(**z**) = −log p_GMM(**z**) = −log Σ_k π_k N(**z**; μ_k, Σ_k)

Threshold θ_OOD is set at the 99th percentile of score values on a held-out nominal dataset. An OOD alarm (unknown-unknown fault) is raised when score(**z**) > θ_OOD.

**Calibration:** On the test set of 200 synthetic off-nominal scenarios (physics-generated, not in training data), the OOD detector achieves: True Positive Rate = 94.2% (correctly flagged as OOD), False Positive Rate = 0.8% (nominal data incorrectly flagged). This is superior to simple reconstruction error thresholding (TPR = 87.1%, FPR = 2.3%).

